(Problem Context: Two university sections have enrolled students in CSE101 and MTH165.) Tj
T*
(Compute: \(1\) Students taking both courses, \(2\) Students taking either course, \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Students in CSE101 only.) Tj
T*
(Python Source Code:) Tj
T*
(cse_students = {'Aarav', 'Diya', 'Rohan', 'Kavita', 'Suresh'}) Tj
T*
(math_students = {'Rohan', 'Kavita', 'Neha', 'Priya', 'Amit'}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(both_courses = cse_students & math_students          # Intersection) Tj
T*
(all_students = cse_students | math_students          # Union) Tj
T*
(cse_only = cse_students - math_students              # Difference) Tj
T*
(exclusive_to_one = cse_students ^ math_students      # Symmetric Difference) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(print\(f'Enrolled in Both \(Intersection\):  {both_courses}'\)) Tj
T*
(print\(f'Total Unique Students \(Union\):     {all_students}'\)) Tj
T*
(print\(f'CSE101 Only \(Difference\):          {cse_only}'\)) Tj
T*
(print\(f'Taking Exactly One Course:         {exclusive_to_one}'\)) Tj
T*
