T*
(* Q1: Contrast lists and tuples in terms of internal memory representation,) Tj
T*
(performance, and mutability.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Lists are mutable dynamic arrays: elements can be modified, appended, or deleted) Tj
T*
(in-place. Because lists must accommodate growth, CPython over-allocates memory slots,) Tj
T*
(incurring extra pointer overhead and reallocation costs. Tuples are immutable: once) Tj
T*
